{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02Z9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F$", "MATH_0002": "$f : V \\to U$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\alpha_V : f^*F(x) \\to F(f^*x)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\beta_V : f^*F(y) \\to F(f^*y)$", "MATH_0006": "$f^*F(x) \\to F(f^*x) \\to F(x)$", "MATH_0007": "$f^*F(x) \\to F(x)$", "MATH_0008": "$\\beta_V$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\mathit{Mor}_{\\mathcal{S}_1}(x, y)(f : V \\to U) \\ar@{=}[r] &\n\\Mor_{\\mathcal{S}_{1, V}}(f^\\ast x, f^\\ast y) \\ar[d] \\\\\n\\mathit{Mor}_{\\mathcal{S}_2}(F(x), F(y))(f : V \\to U) \\ar@{=}[r] &\n\\Mor_{\\mathcal{S}_{2, V}}(f^\\ast F(x), f^\\ast F(y))\n}\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$\\phi \\mapsto \\beta_V^{-1} \\circ F(\\phi) \\circ \\alpha_V$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-definition-fibred-categories-over-C}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:592481581ed33a742c473f325ea5d2cf6f228b20b78cc3de6f791a52dfea65f4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1723c36a0e7b502356e9092471c023166f33dc14d8d8e64f10c8cb5d865a5b0f", "source_text": "By\nCategories, Definition <REF_0001>\nthe functor <MATH_0001> maps strongly cartesian morphisms to strongly cartesian\nmorphisms. Hence if <MATH_0002> is a morphism in <MATH_0003>, then\nthere are canonical isomorphisms <MATH_0004>,\n<MATH_0005> such that <MATH_0006>\nis the canonical morphism <MATH_0007>, and similarly for <MATH_0008>.\nThus we may define\n<MATH_0009>\nby <MATH_0010>.\nWe omit the verification that this is compatible with the restriction\nmappings.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:faf56d43dede3ec8ce27cb043756a99ba9ba14c22cbacd258335cd935a159211", "unit_id": "tag:042V:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks", "node_kind": "remark", "parent_tag": "02Z9", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$p : \\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{S} \\to \\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0003": "$F : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\textit{Groupoids}$", "MATH_0004": "$F$", "MATH_0005": "$g^* \\circ f^* = (f \\circ g)^*$", "MATH_0006": "$\\alpha_{g, f}$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathit{Mor}(x, y)$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-painful}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{categories-lemma-fibred-strict}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-presheaf-mor-map-fibred-categories}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{remark}\n\\label{remark-alternative}\n", "suffix": "\\end{remark}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:42c8b6fb0d5693ea034ae5d26d3feba0f426323009b99882c16968bcf5f8d8a2", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d9dd2c394c14da197777a477bfe93e5427de1fb1a17a779f5306626e8848081e", "source_text": "Suppose that <MATH_0001> is fibred in groupoids.\nIn this case we can prove\nLemma <REF_0001>\nusing\nCategories, Lemma <REF_0002>\nwhich says that <MATH_0002> is equivalent to the\ncategory associated to a contravariant functor\n<MATH_0003>.\nIn the case of the fibred category associated to <MATH_0004>\nwe have <MATH_0005> on the nose\nand there is no need to use the maps <MATH_0006>.\nIn this case the lemma is (even more) trivial. Of course then\none uses that the <MATH_0007> presheaf is\nunchanged when passing to an equivalent fibred category which follows from\nLemma <REF_0003>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:581cefdda07920b6360f9a1560c5c25481b1e3d2374f5b0146bdc9edd20bac9f", "unit_id": "tag:02ZA:statement"}
